   "summary": "Unsealed Monday: DOJ charged former FBI Director James Comey on Oct. 5 by criminal information \u2014 not a grand jury indictment \u2014 with transmitting national defense information and conspiracy tied to an Oct. 2016 New York Times story. His lawyers say it is past the 10-year limit; two earlier U.S. attorney's offices declined. Comey called it \"an appalling abuse of the Department of Justice.\" A prior case was dismissed; he was indicted in North Carolina April 28 over an '8647' post.",
   "firstHand": [
    {
     "who": "James Comey, former FBI Director",
     "role": "Substack video, Oct. 26 (reported by NBC)",
     "url": "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/former-fbi-james-comey-charged-third-time-trump-national-security-rcna342963",
     "quote": "Well, they're back again. It would almost be funny if it weren't such an appalling abuse of the Department of Justice, one that we cannot become numb to."
    }
   ]
